  "content": {
    "id": "p26-q12-root",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "12",
    "prompt": "A car used 30 litres of fuel to travel 105 km. The fuel tank of the car has a capacity of 50 litres. Can the car complete a 180 km journey without refuelling? Give the fuel required to 1 decimal place.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "No. The journey requires approximately $51.4\\text{ L}$, which exceeds the $50\\text{ L}$ tank capacity.",
      "worked": "$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{30\\text{ L}}{105\\text{ km}}&=\\frac{x\\text{ L}}{180\\text{ km}}\\\\x&=\\frac{30\\times180}{105}\\\\x&=\\frac{360}{7}\\\\x&\\approx51.4\\end{align*}$$\nThe journey requires approximately $51.4\\text{ L}$. Since this exceeds the $50\\text{ L}$ tank capacity, the car cannot complete the journey without refuelling.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 34
  },
